    "review_summary": {
      "formal_content": "Reviewed all seven owned pages and the map/reverse-page/translation index entries. The sole inventory binding is saw_p1 / saw_p1_m1, displayed as 骨鋸 外科醫師 型號4; trait identity, icon reference, and shared/reverse links agree.",
      "tier_and_wrapper": "The four own tiers are 0.525/0.55/0.575/0.60. The exact wrapper clones the held-slot conditional base; own values replace the 1.0 fallback. No own proc, stack, or duration is represented.",
      "damage_formula": "The formal equation is F*(S+t): the tier adds to the assembled weakspot/finesse multiplier and affects the base finesse component, not the whole hit. Both controlled examples preserve other terms; the S=1 example and S=1.40 example arithmetic and stated relative increases are correct.",
      "toxin_and_attack_routes": "The toxin weakspot consumer requires melee, weakspot, and the target toxin keyword at damage calculation. Normal coating inserts neurotoxin_interval_buff3; special-active coating inserts saw_rending_debuff; both carry toxin keyword. Attack damage is calculated before its queued coating callback, so first application cannot benefit its own hit. Direct and positive-damage sticky/rip hits each evaluate independently; no same-frame cache ordering guarantee is claimed. Toxin tick is an effect/buff attack and wound visuals are not keyword proof. Push itself and the toggle are excluded; actual melee follow-ups/special-active melee routes remain independently eligible.",
      "raw_and_icon": "The EN/ZH description key, paired RAW hash, formatter source, and I–IV static reconstructions match the registered fractions and prefix; the note correctly says static reconstruction rather than gameplay screenshot. The issue-14 icon receipt confirms the referenced icon asset and verified display.",
      "validation": "All 30 fixed scope files match their SHA-256 values. The scoped focused check reports 41 source ranges across 21 source files, 542 bindings/279 variants, and no new link or GFM errors."
    },
    "limitations": [
      "No live gameplay test was performed; the docs correctly limit claims to source-confirmed conditions and do not promise that a later same-frame sticky hit sees the newly added toxin keyword."
    ]
